            <div class="section"><div class="container"><div class="portfolio p-3-cols simple" id="container"><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="Luzerne County Community College will present A NATURAL DIRECTION, an art exhibition featuring original works inspired by nature by artists Mary Lou Steinberg and Michelle Thomas.

The exhibition will be on display in the Schulman Gallery from Friday, November 13, through Wednesday, December 16, 2026. An opening reception will be held Friday, November 13, from 6:00 to 8:00 p.m., featuring live piano music, light fare and refreshments. Admission is free and open to the public.

The Schulman Gallery is located on the second floor of the Campus Center, Building 14, at LCCC's Nanticoke campus." src="/images/marketing/100.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">A Natural Direction Art Exhibition Opens November 13 at LCCC</strong><p>Luzerne County Community College will present A NATURAL DIRECTION, an art exhibition featuring original works inspired by nature by artists Mary Lou Steinberg and Michelle Thomas.

The exhibition will be on display in the Schulman Gallery from Friday, November 13, through Wednesday, December 16, 2026. An opening reception will be held Friday, November 13, from 6:00 to 8:00 p.m., featuring live piano music, light fare and refreshments. Admission is free and open to the public.

The Schulman Gallery is located on the second floor of the Campus Center, Building 14, at LCCC's Nanticoke campus.<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://www.luzerne.edu/schulmangallery/" tabindex="0" aria-label="A Natural Direction Art Exhibition Opens November 13 at LCCC"><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="The Luzerne County Community College Alumni Association invites the community to its Cash Bingo fundraiser on Sunday, November 15, 2026, at the LCCC Campus Center, 521 Trailblazer Drive, Nanticoke.

The event will feature 20 games of bingo, special games, raffles, basket prizes, door prizes and a 50/50 drawing. DJ Rob Sax will serve as the bingo caller, and food will be available for purchase on a cash-only basis.

Doors open at 11:30 a.m., with bingo beginning at 1 p.m. Admission is $25 per person, and seating is limited.

Advance registration is required. No tickets will be sold at the door.

Sponsorship opportunities are available. For tickets or additional information, contact the LCCC Alumni Association at 570-740-0734 or blzuer@luzerne.edu.

Join the LCCC Alumni Association for an afternoon of bingo, prizes and community fun while supporting the College's alumni community." src="/images/marketing/99.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">LCCC Alumni Association to Host Cash Bingo on November 15</strong><p>The Luzerne County Community College Alumni Association invites the community to its Cash Bingo fundraiser on Sunday, November 15, 2026, at the LCCC Campus Center, 521 Trailblazer Drive, Nanticoke.

The event will feature 20 games of bingo, special games, raffles, basket prizes, door prizes and a 50/50 drawing. DJ Rob Sax will serve as the bingo caller, and food will be available for purchase on a cash-only basis.

Doors open at 11:30 a.m., with bingo beginning at 1 p.m. Admission is $25 per person, and seating is limited.

Advance registration is required. No tickets will be sold at the door.

Sponsorship opportunities are available. For tickets or additional information, contact the LCCC Alumni Association at 570-740-0734 or <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="b6d4daccc3d3c4f6dac3ccd3c4d8d398d3d2c3">[email&#160;protected]</a>.

Join the LCCC Alumni Association for an afternoon of bingo, prizes and community fun while supporting the College's alumni community.<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://lp.constantcontactpages.com/ev/reg/g5yqzzm/lp/65631b19-c394-48b1-9403-1dba3f9914b6" tabindex="0" aria-label="LCCC Alumni Association to Host Cash Bingo on November 15"><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="The new L3C Microcredential Academy brings accessible, career-focused healthcare training to communities across LCCC’s eight locations in four counties.
From CNA and EMT to Phlebotomy, EKG, Medical Assistant and other in-demand healthcare credentials, the Academy provides multiple entry points to rewarding careers and opportunities to build skills over time.
Eight Locations. One Workforce Mission.
" src="/images/marketing/97.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">L3C Microcredential Academy</strong><p>The new L3C Microcredential Academy brings accessible, career-focused healthcare training to communities across LCCC’s eight locations in four counties.
From CNA and EMT to Phlebotomy, EKG, Medical Assistant and other in-demand healthcare credentials, the Academy provides multiple entry points to rewarding careers and opportunities to build skills over time.
Eight Locations. One Workforce Mission.
<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://www.luzerne.edu/micro/" tabindex="0" aria-label="L3C Microcredential Academy"><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="The Pennsylvania Municipal Police Officers' Education and Training Commission (MPOETC) has approved Luzerne County Community College (LCCC) to operate one of Pennsylvania’s newest Act 120 Municipal Police Academies. The academy will be housed at LCCC’s Public Safety Training Institute in Nanticoke and will begin in spring 2027, offering two cohorts of 25 cadets each.

" src="/images/marketing/34.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">Luzerne County Community College Designated as Pennsylvania’s Newest Act 120 Municipal Police Academy</strong><p>The Pennsylvania Municipal Police Officers' Education and Training Commission (MPOETC) has approved Luzerne County Community College (LCCC) to operate one of Pennsylvania’s newest Act 120 Municipal Police Academies. The academy will be housed at LCCC’s Public Safety Training Institute in Nanticoke and will begin in spring 2027, offering two cohorts of 25 cadets each.

<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://www.luzerne.edu/act120/" tabindex="0" aria-label="Luzerne County Community College Designated as Pennsylvania’s Newest Act 120 Municipal Police Academy"><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="Discover how Luzerne County Community College’s Career & Technology Academy is preparing students for high-demand careers and fueling Pennsylvania’s workforce. Click below to watch a statewide feature from PMA Perspective." src="/images/marketing/60.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">Career & Technology Academy</strong><p>Discover how Luzerne County Community College’s Career & Technology Academy is preparing students for high-demand careers and fueling Pennsylvania’s workforce. Click below to watch a statewide feature from PMA Perspective.<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://pamanufacturers.org/pma-perspective/luzerne-county-community-college-training-pennsylvanias-workforce/" tabindex="0" aria-label="Career & Technology Academy"><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="Luzerne County Community College (LCCC), Commonwealth University of Pennsylvania (CU), and Hazleton Area School District (HASD) are launching an educational partnership in Fall 2025 to tackle Pennsylvania's critical teacher shortage, where over 5,500 vacancies exist amidst declining education degree enrollments and record teacher attrition." src="/images/marketing/39.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">TEACH IN NEPA</strong><p>Luzerne County Community College (LCCC), Commonwealth University of Pennsylvania (CU), and Hazleton Area School District (HASD) are launching an educational partnership in Fall 2025 to tackle Pennsylvania's critical teacher shortage, where over 5,500 vacancies exist amidst declining education degree enrollments and record teacher attrition.<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://www.luzerne.edu/teachinnepaproject/" tabindex="0" aria-label="TEACH IN NEPA"><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div><div class="portfolio-item develop"><img alt="Luzerne County Community College (LCCC) and Misericordia University (MU) today announced a new, innovative transfer policy that formally recognizes the academic value of an associate degree earned at LCCC and significantly simplifies the transfer process for students pursuing a bachelor’s degree at Misericordia University.

Under the new policy, students who complete an Associate of Arts (AA) or Associate of Science (AS) Degree at LCCC will have Misericordia University’s undergraduate core curriculum requirements waived upon transfer. This means students can move more directly into coursework for their chosen major, reducing both the time and cost associated with earning a four-year degree." src="/images/marketing/77.jpg" ><div class="name-holder"><strong style="font-size:16px;color:#004685;">LCCC and Misericordia University Announce Innovative Transfer Policy </strong><p>Luzerne County Community College (LCCC) and Misericordia University (MU) today announced a new, innovative transfer policy that formally recognizes the academic value of an associate degree earned at LCCC and significantly simplifies the transfer process for students pursuing a bachelor’s degree at Misericordia University.

Under the new policy, students who complete an Associate of Arts (AA) or Associate of Science (AS) Degree at LCCC will have Misericordia University’s undergraduate core curriculum requirements waived upon transfer. This means students can move more directly into coursework for their chosen major, reducing both the time and cost associated with earning a four-year degree.<br><div class="highlight"><a href="https://www.luzerne.edu/about/news/more.jsp?id=37" tabindex="0" aria-label="LCCC and Misericordia University Announce Innovative Transfer Policy "><strong>READ MORE</strong></a></div></div></div></div></div></div>
            
				<div class="section main-bg" style="padding:30px 0" data-stellar-background-ratio="0.6">
					<div class="container">
						<div class="cta_btn">
							
							<div class="f-left">
								<h2 class="cta_heading bold white">Northeastern Pennsylvania's Community College</h2>
								<h4 class="cta_heading white">LCCC has the largest population in northeastern PA making Luzerne the area's <span style="font-size:18px;font-weight:bolder;color:white">#1 choice!</span>.</h4>
							</div>    
							
